#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|act=V|scene=ii|page=97|column=1|passage=Commend me to them, <br> And tell them, that to eaſe them of their greefes, <br> Their feares of Hoſtile ſtrokes, their Aches loſſes, <br> Their pangs of Loue, with other incident '''throwes''' <br> That Natures fragile Veſſell doth ſuſtaine <br> In lifes vncertaine voyage, I will ſome kindnes do them, {{...}}}}
